# j6a run-condition test: fixture outputs, captured 2026-10-02 ~14:00 UTC

The test is AUDIT/post-f-2026-10-02/j6a_cond_test.sh. It extracts the fsucc run-condition block
from box_q_j6a.sh and runs it against 16 fixtures. Each fixture sets fsucc's word, the
human's advance pin and the fsucc decision JSON. The test checks whether the block reaches the
run path or defers.

## OLD=1: the block at main 2663141, before Fable's amendment (lines 78-83)

The test fails exactly the new case.

    FAIL room_only_with_pin: expected run got defer
        === j6a DEFERRED to the re-plan: fsucc's word is 'refused', not quiet (Fable Q2: j6a runs only if fsucc was quiet)
    pass=15 fail=1

## The amended block (lines 82-106)

    PASS quiet (run)
    PASS quiet_no_pin_needed (run)
    PASS room_only_with_pin (run)
    PASS room_only_no_pin (defer)
    PASS room_only_empty_pin (defer)
    PASS room_and_b (defer)
    PASS room_no_arms (defer)
    PASS arms_not_object (defer)
    PASS both_win_a (defer)
    PASS empty_reasons (defer)
    PASS no_detail (defer)
    PASS refused_no_json (defer)
    PASS fires_j6f (defer)
    PASS fires_j6dv4 (defer)
    PASS absent_word (defer)
    PASS malformed_word (defer)
    pass=16 fail=0

On both versions, `bash -n` passes. `shellcheck -x -S warning` reports nothing on the amended
file.

## Not tested here

- The two F′-ledger checks use absolute box paths (/home/ubuntu/ledger/gh200-fsucc-*.jsonl).
  Those paths do not exist on the Mac, so on the Mac those checks always pass.
- The JSON is the shape qd-post-f-rules-succ writes. That is read from
  `qd_post_f_rules.rs` `settle`/`finish`: `detail.arms`, plus `detail.refused_because` as a list
  of reasons tagged "(c)"/"(b)"/"(a)". The test does not use a real fsucc JSON, because none
  exists yet.
